    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d92">

                <pb facs="0216" n="102" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg102"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">422.11Am8/36: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hartman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-03-13T15:00:00-05:14"><hi rendition="#italic">March 13,
                                1922—3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March 14—1:20
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>8. Department’s 6, March 1, 4 p.m.</p>
                <p>Ecuadorean Government in reply reiterates statements contained in my despatch
                    number 767 [<hi rendition="#italic">761?</hi>] December 1st<anchor n="9"
                        xml:id="d92-f1"/> and adds diplomatic intervention only justified in case of
                    judicial denial of justice. Full report by mail.<anchor n="10" xml:id="d92-f2"
                    /></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hartman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
